# One author, several addresses. Maps every commit to the identity the repository commits under
# today, so `git shortlog` and `git blame` name one person rather than several. The history itself is
# unchanged — this file only changes how it is displayed. An address that is not the project's own is
# mapped in a local, untracked file (`git config mailmap.file`), not here: this repository is public.
